<node id="Predicates">
  <data key="d0">Predicates</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Predicates are elements used in processing sub-contexts within micro context.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional words such as knowing, going, to, for that shape the central search intent and appear in content.&lt;SEP&gt;Predicates are words like "time", "spend", and "time spending" that indicate semantic roles in the answer.&lt;SEP&gt;Predicates are specific verbs or phrases (e.g., improve, increase, affect) that must appear in paragraphs.&lt;SEP&gt;Predicates are grammatical elements that can be verbs or instructions, used in structuring content for SEO.&lt;SEP&gt;Predicates are linguistic elements that signal contextual connections, with some marked as bold in the content item brief design.&lt;SEP&gt;Words like generate, create, make, adjust, add, branding, etc., that signal contextual transitions between subsections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a2c4e2ae1837755693d47d4e276e0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e7da857e573232b8497dce8e12f896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66b6eab94f52b9bb0e353a781becd4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7299ff5f066dee74796eab27e8c910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ad6b0780f4ae2de415293f3a5c7c523&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e516c24df7f67e764c86da19d203579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbedcd7bd86eeb3e840ab8d2ece81dfa</data>
