<node id="Internal Link">
  <data key="d0">Internal Link</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A hyperlink within the website that connects pages, used to reinforce the central search intent.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal links connect articles, with macro and micro contexts interchanging between them.&lt;SEP&gt;A hyperlink connecting two pages within the same website, used when the same word appears in different URL paths to indicate a relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;An Internal Link is a hyperlink connecting one page of a website to another, used to connect macro and micro contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal link is a hyperlink pointing to another page within the same domain, its quantity increases when moving lower in the hierarchy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8e7da857e573232b8497dce8e12f896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d827ad12e77bd39e3b9d93257eb0019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84be65ef542a67b8c7039f750beecb23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6fcf117c831329dacb93b241158f58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ee2eb6040df1e6c4d380a109521b50</data>
