<node id="Lexical Relations">
  <data key="d0">Lexical Relations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The relationships between words, such as hypernymy and hyponymy, relevant to understanding title tag structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Lexical Relations are semantic connections between words, such as antonyms, used to increase relevance.&lt;SEP&gt;Lexical Relations are semantic relationships between words, used to infer group practice from individual practice.&lt;SEP&gt;Lexical relations are semantic connections between terms, which the lecturer avoids expanding on to prevent context dilution.&lt;SEP&gt;Relationships between words, such as hyponyms, used in query networks.</data>
