<node id="Methodology">
  <data key="d0">Methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The instructor's approach to writing URLs, which avoids repeating words and uses single or two-word top-level segments, and creates internal links between repeated words.&lt;SEP&gt;The methodology is the systematic approach used in the article.&lt;SEP&gt;The methodology encompasses the contextual vector, general summary, and internal links, all together.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84be65ef542a67b8c7039f750beecb23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9819cf025207d885301e2eb37c93e99e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1ae1f1b49055c6666741019f9fa17ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779796077</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Life">
  <data key="d0">Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A topic used in the URL structure example, under which culture and religion are placed in the context of Germany.&lt;SEP&gt;Life is a category in the topical map under which the population of Germany is placed, connected to culture and visas.&lt;SEP&gt;Life is a term that is important as a benefit provided by water, and authors are helped to use it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84be65ef542a67b8c7039f750beecb23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1ae1f1b49055c6666741019f9fa17ae</data>
