<node id="Headings">
  <data key="d0">Headings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Headings are HTML elements used to structure content, with some headings introducing supplementary topics.&lt;SEP&gt;HTML headings used to structure content, sometimes containing anchor text.&lt;SEP&gt;Headings are used to structure the article, and the author is not allowed to change them.&lt;SEP&gt;HTML heading elements (H2s) used to structure content and signal topic relevance to search engines.&lt;SEP&gt;Headings are the titles and subtitles used in an article, outlined in the content brief.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6fcf117c831329dacb93b241158f58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eef1d53ea2fafdb6002975ead6658b03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-291afa9bbbeab0842d299e3a83bd26b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c416bcd7aedd056158284b55f461171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff65f727135659538eed14f8dcf24d1f</data>
