<node id="Knowledge Domain">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Domain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Knowledge domain is a topical area where multiple websites compete for authority and rankings.&lt;SEP&gt;A Knowledge Domain represents a specific area of knowledge, used in constructing topical maps.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific area of knowledge for knowledge base construction.&lt;SEP&gt;A knowledge domain is a specific field of expertise that an author may or may not be deeply familiar with.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6cb0443852c88f9233a38374df7483b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-601527952de3e4cb533d4928c1d0ad26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052d6944053b5b3df8d3057ea51f965e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89ba62f2b9f725725fe8219a87ffad3</data>
