  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Root Article">
  <data key="d0">Root Article</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A Root Article is a central piece of content that connects to the most important things and is linked back from them, forming the basis of the internal link structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Root article is the primary article created from the most prominent, popular, and relevant attribute, such as population of Germany.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-043bc92a7015e647914eacacd758a036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791965</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anchor Tags">
  <data key="d0">Anchor Tags</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Anchor Tags are the HTML elements used for internal links, with specific anchor text chosen for SEO.&lt;SEP&gt;HTML elements used in content that may need updating when content items are changed or reordered.&lt;SEP&gt;Anchor tags are HTML elements used to create connections between sections.&lt;SEP&gt;HTML elements used to link to specific sections, such as ways to test pH.&lt;SEP&gt;HTML anchor tags used in the article, to be discussed in the next lecture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-043bc92a7015e647914eacacd758a036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ead1494c17202662c334ce26d68202b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de13c628f8d2f506d2b52782fc3a99f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-237f0369c76d4e73efce226fd0388537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8f3737ebb9deefae951ea2e92ccc158</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779809026</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SEO">
  <data key="d0">SEO</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SEO (Search Engine Optimization) is the practice of optimizing content to rank higher in search engines, and the framework aids in remembering to insert internal links.&lt;SEP&gt;Search Engine Optimization, the practice of improving website visibility.&lt;SEP&gt;SEO is the field of search engine optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;SEO (Search Engine Optimization) is the practice of optimizing content to rank higher in search engines, with a future methodology involving language models and human effort.&lt;SEP&gt;SEO (Search Engine Optimization) is a field where understanding is more important than imitation, and involves creating content based on semantic connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-043bc92a7015e647914eacacd758a036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052d6944053b5b3df8d3057ea51f965e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8122ad3e878784e98cdd0c33cb998553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a99a29e62de16c6682606a21ab6928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87e7258feb16ea29ce55cfb202887445</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779809764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crawlers">
  <data key="d0">Crawlers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Crawlers are search engine bots that index web pages, and internal links in main content give them heavier weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-043bc92a7015e647914eacacd758a036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791657</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Page Shrink Flow">
  <data key="d0">Page Shrink Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Page Shrink Flow is a concept related to how link weight flows through a site, influenced by internal link placement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-043bc92a7015e647914eacacd758a036</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791657</data>
