<node id="Contextual Domain">
  <data key="d0">Contextual Domain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Contextual Domain unites different knowledge domains based on shared entities, attributes, and purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific topic area where deeper content is allowed in certain sections.&lt;SEP&gt;The Contextual Domain is the broader thematic area surrounding the drinking hot water topic.&lt;SEP&gt;Contextual domain is a specific subsection created for natural language inferring occurrences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-601527952de3e4cb533d4928c1d0ad26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad882cdccd8e0beb9a3d86482839006&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-693450104ff13d2ef5a1111365e8c7e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b6216c51b8b71b22fb85e4c681c6c2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779801768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Distance">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Distance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic Distance is the measure of separation between knowledge domains, shaping the topical map.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-601527952de3e4cb533d4928c1d0ad26</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791787</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query">
  <data key="d0">Query</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Query is a search term or phrase that contains functional words, concrete words, and user inquiry intent.&lt;SEP&gt;A search query that users ask; AI systems retrieve documents to answer it.&lt;SEP&gt;A query is a search term that may be used to generate questions and internal links in a content brief.&lt;SEP&gt;A query is a search query that may exist for one country but not another, used in synthetic search queries.&lt;SEP&gt;A search query, such as "what are the benefits of drinking a gallon of water every day".</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-601527952de3e4cb533d4928c1d0ad26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa4f955c977e4411acda6af90a1e984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575a42261e7ed1bc18d072052828622&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-721fd7360c4042bb96070adb318d92eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-523ebf9e23d3cd025d58126d5ea07ab8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779796748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Word">
  <data key="d0">Functional Word</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Functional Word is a component of a query that serves a grammatical or structural purpose.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional Word is a word like "via" that connects concepts in sentence structures, with drinking water coming after it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-601527952de3e4cb533d4928c1d0ad26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7299ff5f066dee74796eab27e8c910</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779796361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concrete Word">
  <data key="d0">Concrete Word</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Concrete Word is a component of a query that represents a tangible entity or attribute.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-601527952de3e4cb533d4928c1d0ad26</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791787</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Inquiry Intent">
  <data key="d0">User Inquiry Intent</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">User Inquiry Intent is the underlying goal or need expressed in a search query.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-601527952de3e4cb533d4928c1d0ad26</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791787</data>
