<node id="Attribute Criterias">
  <data key="d0">Attribute Criterias</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attribute Criterias are standards used to filter entity attributes for content brief creation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-601527952de3e4cb533d4928c1d0ad26</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791788</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attribute Filtration">
  <data key="d0">Attribute Filtration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Attribute filtration is the process of filtering attributes inside queries, discussed in the 16th lecture, with three criteria: prominence, popularity, and relevance.&lt;SEP&gt;Attribute filtration is a process mentioned in the context of content brief creation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0632b547a34e2bc896a85a73634711</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779805244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entity Attribute">
  <data key="d0">Entity Attribute</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Entity attribute is a characteristic of an entity, part of entity-attribute-value triples, and understanding it is aided by a video and article.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Value Triples">
  <data key="d0">Value Triples</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Value triples are the combination of entity, attribute, and value, mentioned as something to understand for filtering attributes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attribute Prominence">
  <data key="d0">Attribute Prominence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attribute prominence is a criterion for attribute filtration, derived from the definition of the entity; an attribute is prominent if removing it would change the entity's fundamental definition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Football League">
  <data key="d0">Football League</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Football league is an attribute of Germany that is not prominent but is popular, and not relevant to the source context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basketball League">
  <data key="d0">Basketball League</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basketball league is another attribute of Germany similar to football league, not prominent but popular.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attribute Popularity">
  <data key="d0">Attribute Popularity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attribute popularity is a criterion for attribute filtration, determined by search demand; an attribute is popular if it is frequently searched.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791937</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attribute Relevance">
  <data key="d0">Attribute Relevance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attribute relevance is a criterion for attribute filtration, defined by relevance to the source context rather than to the entity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779791938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="H1">
  <data key="d0">H1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">H1 is an HTML heading tag that serves as the main heading of a webpage or document, reflecting the macro context, central entity, and central search intent of the content. It typically contains specific context terms that define the topical map and signal the primary topic to both users and search engines. In a specific lecture context, H1 is discussed through a series of illustrative and somewhat unconventional examples: the instructor questions why the term “population” is not placed directly inside the H1, notes that the appearance of an internet extension within an H1 triggers a contextual question, and humorously remarks that H1 mainly contains water, citing instances such as “hot water” as a primary topic. These examples serve to emphasize the role of the H1 tag as a macro context signifier and a structural element that encapsulates the overarching theme of the content.&lt;SEP&gt;H1 is the main heading of a webpage, part of the macro context area.&lt;SEP&gt;The H1 is the top-level heading in the article.&lt;SEP&gt;H1 is a heading level that unifies the content of its subordinate H2 headings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad882cdccd8e0beb9a3d86482839006&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f812c017168e90729b20b23af0336de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2101b749bdada7714a4bb5ee41a942c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a388368023eee5caf3dbbc03fcdd278d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8122ad3e878784e98cdd0c33cb998553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c77ed812b87a04f08a3ce700769524d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c10223fd9ea5d44bdbd29c6221184f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab08862cb455a716bef38bcdb6db556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-291afa9bbbeab0842d299e3a83bd26b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9edf2abec867ee2a44168ee963aa04e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779808257</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lecturer">
  <data key="d0">Lecturer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The lecturer is the speaker of the 16th lecture, who keeps the content practical and suggests additional resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The lecturer is the instructor of the Semantic SEO course, who published the Saigon speech about the future of SEO.&lt;SEP&gt;The lecturer is the speaker delivering the 43rd lecture, providing instructions on content methodology and SEO practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The lecturer is the instructor of the Semantic SEO course, who delivered the Saigon speech and shares insights on SEO, seconds modeling, and content structuring.&lt;SEP&gt;The lecturer is the speaker delivering the lecture, guiding the examination of various concepts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lecturer is the instructor of the Semantic SEO course, delivering the 67th lecture on macro context creation and discourse integration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lecturer is the person giving the lecture, using instructions in a brief way, and providing article revision videos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beff6e5691c00d2a3ced912957383f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044463b06024487bc6e52187cb1877de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b39188a27a68c4df8a21ff349b5a66ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45a2a27d5f61609219a67e6c845917a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1adac99c2781316b94ff37456478c25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3274b5b11d4b886cb9e0202f9dee7f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc3b08eaa821f490808f28acdb3427f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779804091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
