<node id="Contextual Flow">
  <data key="d0">Contextual Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contextual flow explains where context is taken from and where it is led to in a document, guiding the order of anchor texts and the overall structure.&lt;SEP&gt;A component of the contextual structure methodology that determines the flow of the content.&lt;SEP&gt;Contextual flow is the logical connection between sections, achieved by using common phrases and themes.&lt;SEP&gt;Contextual flow is the structure of providing information: when it is seen, how to observe, how to prevent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6aa4f955c977e4411acda6af90a1e984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a2bd575df4c8a0d322e5adcf2e78bc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f678064163d41d8196871b5a23c9069c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b15cca57f0ab0737789ae9524b989e9a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779803927</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contextual Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Contextual Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contextual coverage explains which part of an article is the heaviest or most important, determining the focus of summarization and content weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Contextual coverage is the balance of content depth to avoid redundancy and maintain relevance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6aa4f955c977e4411acda6af90a1e984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a862d8cd031c8ba43a92cd09c11ae3b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779800863</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ai Summarizer">
  <data key="d0">Ai Summarizer</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An AI system that summarizes articles; its effectiveness depends on understanding contextual coverage to capture the main purpose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6aa4f955c977e4411acda6af90a1e984</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779793009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge Base">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Base</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A collection of information that can be verbalized and improved; organizing it requires understanding contextual flow and coverage.&lt;SEP&gt;A repository of facts used to verify declarations and generate content.&lt;SEP&gt;A knowledge base is a repository of information where defining the most important section leads to higher relevance.&lt;SEP&gt;A knowledge base is being constructed by overlapping contexts and linking pages.&lt;SEP&gt;A knowledge base is a repository of facts, with some containing billions of facts, that can be verbalized into text to create expert-level websites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6aa4f955c977e4411acda6af90a1e984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9c9ba387025eda6de114e2f950fa53c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89ba62f2b9f725725fe8219a87ffad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2002fbb248a146a783e2d25d0a26b5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87e7258feb16ea29ce55cfb202887445</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779809765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query Network">
  <data key="d0">Query Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Query Network is a structured set of interconnected search queries that are relevant to a specific topic, entity, or its attributes. It encompasses not only primary queries but also their variations, forming a comprehensive map of the search landscape that a website or piece of content aims to target. This network is derived from the core entity and its characteristics, ensuring that the collection of queries is both topically coherent and contextually rich.

Functionally, the Query Network serves as a framework for content creation and structuring. It guides the development of articles by determining the weight and directional emphasis of context, which justifies why certain sections—such as a particular disease area in a medical article—receive more coverage or prominence. By analyzing the network, content strategists can structure material to directly match user intent and the specific queries being searched. Thus, the Query Network is both a diagnostic tool for understanding topical demand and a prescriptive blueprint for organizing information to satisfy that demand effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Query network is a targeted network of queries and terms used to improve relevance.&lt;SEP&gt;A network of connected queries that influences the weight of content sections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6aa4f955c977e4411acda6af90a1e984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f812c017168e90729b20b23af0336de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a388368023eee5caf3dbbc03fcdd278d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-523ebf9e23d3cd025d58126d5ea07ab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dacc856640e50f4d171e6fe531e33d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81b837e1fc804bb7df2114c65c3758ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ad6b0780f4ae2de415293f3a5c7c523&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a862d8cd031c8ba43a92cd09c11ae3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d85e10b2285c1072884beb02946f33e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56cdab63084565b9b40cd1b6dfaa1d57</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779803116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extractive Summary">
  <data key="d0">Extractive Summary</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A summary created by selecting the most important sentences from different sections; a proper contextual flow ensures the article can represent itself.&lt;SEP&gt;Extractive summary is a method of summarization discussed in the lecture, created from an article.&lt;SEP&gt;Extractive Summary is a summary created by extracting and modifying key sentences from different subsections of an article.&lt;SEP&gt;Extractive summary is a method of creating summaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6aa4f955c977e4411acda6af90a1e984&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbac222e7b9f4ed501578b6503d7e819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c6c0977e83a555c288951c70d42e339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8122ad3e878784e98cdd0c33cb998553</data>
