<node id="Contextual Domains">
  <data key="d0">Contextual Domains</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A concept explained in the lecture, synonymous or related to knowledge basis, referring to domains of context.&lt;SEP&gt;Contextual Domains are the overarching themes or areas (e.g., physical performance, drinking water) that must be covered.&lt;SEP&gt;Contextual domains refer to the distribution of contextual terms within an article, as discussed in the previous lecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Contextual domains are thematic areas that define the context of content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c014d35d8d2fc2d10ceb8a1f6a08dde8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7299ff5f066dee74796eab27e8c910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c77ed812b87a04f08a3ce700769524d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d85e10b2285c1072884beb02946f33e</data>
