<node id="Water">
  <data key="d0">Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water is a central entity within a project, where it serves as the primary example in a topical map and appears as a main topic under H1 headings. It is discussed in lectures, featured in example articles, and used as a term that appears across all sections of a webpage, demonstrating its page-wide relevance.

The substance is characterized by a set of attributes that include its benefits, recommended amount, and various types. Its pH is identified as a root attribute, and the quality and associated benefits of water are influenced by its different types and sources. Among the specific types mentioned are mineral water, luxury water, Arctic water, and lemon water, among others.

In the context of health and nutrition, water is noted for having zero calories and performing a range of functions. It is associated with multiple health benefits, including the practice of drinking water in the morning, and these benefits are supported by referenced studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is a substance that, when consumed, has various health effects such as improving brain function and treating constipation.&lt;SEP&gt;The natural substance that is a major component of plasma and blood, essential for bodily functions like temperature regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is a topic used in search examples, such as searching for PDF files about water from educational websites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb0d0818187343a7c01c321335563cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f812c017168e90729b20b23af0336de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044463b06024487bc6e52187cb1877de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2101b749bdada7714a4bb5ee41a942c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad49d2ec5b75756ff8ac96a9e0a07d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d3b62e9a672b017589bbc9685367180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b005d420a23cdcba2ecafc2a1d59783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b6216c51b8b71b22fb85e4c681c6c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aea7abfa9cae709ad280790ed42d424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c416bcd7aedd056158284b55f461171&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec8e7c18c9c9fd7ef5951e6635b00e42</data>
