  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A predicate is a context term, adjective, or verb chosen to connect an entity and attribute within a topical map.&lt;SEP&gt;A predicate is an important element to define when detailing a central entity in the methodology.&lt;SEP&gt;A grammatical term; drinking water is used as a predicate in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;Predicate refers to the part of a sentence that expresses an action or state, varied in questions to target different query networks.&lt;SEP&gt;A part of the query structure, used in the contextual vector.</data>
