<node id="Contextual Vectors">
  <data key="d0">Contextual Vectors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contextual vectors are ordered lists of terms that represent context for content optimization, discussed in the lecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Elements within the topical map that are not sharpened or deepened.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e01ed3aea772496ae6d36729867a557&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46709e42ef223e72db78ae1e1048c87</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779810712</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Incremental Order Heating List">
  <data key="d0">Incremental Order Heating List</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An incremental order heating list is a method for creating feature snippets, where items are ordered by importance using numeric values, with the total number signaled in the heading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e01ed3aea772496ae6d36729867a557</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779795436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Candidate Passage Answer Creation">
  <data key="d0">Candidate Passage Answer Creation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Candidate passage answer creation is a process for generating potential answers for feature snippets, focusing on passage ranking and scoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e01ed3aea772496ae6d36729867a557</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779795436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Passage Ranking">
  <data key="d0">Passage Ranking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Passage ranking is a method used to evaluate and order passages for quality in content optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Passage ranking is a search engine feature that ranks individual passages from web pages, developed to surface quality content from massive pages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e01ed3aea772496ae6d36729867a557&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc8869133cffd3a4667b0bce46eca871</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779797512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scoring">
  <data key="d0">Scoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scoring is a method used to assign values to passages to determine their relevance and quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e01ed3aea772496ae6d36729867a557</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779795436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Passage">
  <data key="d0">Quality Passage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A quality passage is a well-crafted piece of content that improves the overall quality of a website.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e01ed3aea772496ae6d36729867a557</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779795436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Performance">
  <data key="d0">Physical Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical performance is a key concept in the contextual vector, often placed first due to its importance and connection to queries about water benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical Performance is a concept related to abilities like running, swimming, walking, working, which can be improved by drinking water.&lt;SEP&gt;A term that can have multiple meanings; in the lecture, it is defined from a medical point of view.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical Performance is a context term used in articles, identified via the Multi-Search Extension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e01ed3aea772496ae6d36729867a557&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7299ff5f066dee74796eab27e8c910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aea7abfa9cae709ad280790ed42d424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-176ba103322e465c5c762eb258005dd2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779809719</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="H2">
  <data key="d0">H2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">H2 is a second-level heading used as a bridge between main content and supplementary content.&lt;SEP&gt;H2 is an HTML heading tag used to structure content, forming sub-articles when followed by H3 or H4 tags.&lt;SEP&gt;H2 is a heading level in HTML used to structure content sections, with multiple H2s representing different directions in the contextual vector.&lt;SEP&gt;H2 is a heading level used in content structure to organize sections.&lt;SEP&gt;H2 is a heading level whose content is unified under an H1 heading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a388368023eee5caf3dbbc03fcdd278d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc8869133cffd3a4667b0bce46eca871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce47151a2b89b01b7efea15668a4972c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab08862cb455a716bef38bcdb6db556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9edf2abec867ee2a44168ee963aa04e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779808258</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bridge">
  <data key="d0">Bridge</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The bridge is a heading that acts as a border between macro context/main content and micro contexts/supplementary content, often an H2.&lt;SEP&gt;A connecting element that leads from the symptoms hidden list to supplementary content.&lt;SEP&gt;A transitional element in the article that connects the main topic to related subjects, such as animal bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;A connecting element that has a connection with the situation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a388368023eee5caf3dbbc03fcdd278d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47038fb631de71b9ded57fb5328deec5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46a5ce46cdcaba690c43278c43e6956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e416e4151ad065b84215660d6d94148a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779799897</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Numeric Value Content">
  <data key="d0">Numeric Value Content</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Numeric value content includes numbers, and linking from such content to numeric articles helps ranking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a388368023eee5caf3dbbc03fcdd278d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779795608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boolean Questions">
  <data key="d0">Boolean Questions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Boolean questions are yes/no questions used in supplementary content to focus on contextual layers.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean Questions are questions that can be answered with yes or no, often used for voice search.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean questions are yes/no type queries that appear infrequently in the query network and are not directly used in the macro context.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean questions are direct questions that often use should and are answered with suggestions.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean questions are a type of question used in content, particularly in areas discussing opposites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a388368023eee5caf3dbbc03fcdd278d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6ee67e32c07c0182dd83e65b717d89d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dacc856640e50f4d171e6fe531e33d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d3998f031b7e8a52781909a7faa1829&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d812dd7762edcda121f56954dea1223f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779808746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antonym Context">
  <data key="d0">Antonym Context</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antonym context refers to opposite topics used in supplementary content, such as dehydration vs. drinking water.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a388368023eee5caf3dbbc03fcdd278d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779795609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dehydration">
  <data key="d0">Dehydration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dehydration is a physiological state defined by an inadequate amount of water in the body, standing in direct opposition to overhydration or water intoxication. It is a condition that commonly triggers constipation and is broadly linked to poor digestive health, as evidenced by research studies. The body's need for drinking water is directly influenced by dehydration, and the condition itself is effectively prevented through adequate water intake. In certain content contexts, dehydration has been employed as an antonym for drinking water and was previously a focal point in content briefs. Additionally, dehydration is recognized as a health effect that can be associated with cold water consumption, though the precise nature of this relationship may vary. Overall, dehydration represents a critical imbalance in body water that impacts multiple aspects of health and is frequently contrasted with states of proper hydration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a388368023eee5caf3dbbc03fcdd278d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7299ff5f066dee74796eab27e8c910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ead1494c17202662c334ce26d68202b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f678064163d41d8196871b5a23c9069c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aea7abfa9cae709ad280790ed42d424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22c59e2a7169d4f33e0aa485c94cdfc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c762de7be0b6a4d90e049c5181bbfa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-176ba103322e465c5c762eb258005dd2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779809736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hierarchy">
  <data key="d0">Hierarchy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hierarchy refers to a structured order, where going lower increases the amount of internal links from the bottom.&lt;SEP&gt;Hierarchy refers to the structural organization of content, to be covered in the next lecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Hierarchy is a structural concept examined together with contextual vector and structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Hierarchy is a structural concept used in organizing content within the semantic content network.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1ee2eb6040df1e6c4d380a109521b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dacc856640e50f4d171e6fe531e33d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1adac99c2781316b94ff37456478c25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e516c24df7f67e764c86da19d203579</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779807373</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
