<node id="Micro Semantics">
  <data key="d0">Micro Semantics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The fine-grained semantic elements like word proximities, co-occurrences, sequences, discourse integration, and semantic role labels that determine ranking.&lt;SEP&gt;The detailed semantic meaning derived from micro context, often supplementary.&lt;SEP&gt;Detailed semantics that are part of the supplementary content.&lt;SEP&gt;Micro semantics is a detailed semantic layer that complements macro semantics in content organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Micro Semantics is a concept related to large language models and AI, expected to become more prominent in SEO.&lt;SEP&gt;Micro semantics refers to the detailed sentence structures and word choices used to compete in search engine rankings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a2bd575df4c8a0d322e5adcf2e78bc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47038fb631de71b9ded57fb5328deec5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ead1494c17202662c334ce26d68202b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c10223fd9ea5d44bdbd29c6221184f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b995c5d7fab964c7a148a75f0272e270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9ca968c07a96f9bfe4f63b31908aca6</data>
