<node id="Drinking Too Much Water">
  <data key="d0">Drinking Too Much Water</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A health condition and macro context topic, associated with risks and water intoxication.&lt;SEP&gt;Drinking too much water is an action that is equivalent to water intoxication.&lt;SEP&gt;Drinking too much water is the central context term that flows throughout the entire webpage, appearing in every subsection.&lt;SEP&gt;The act of consuming excessive amounts of water, which can lead to various health issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Drinking too much water is an action that leads to water intoxication and is a recurring contextual phrase in the content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ead1494c17202662c334ce26d68202b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcaf9e38bb2a570a6edf70e6a9681dfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c77ed812b87a04f08a3ce700769524d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22c59e2a7169d4f33e0aa485c94cdfc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b15cca57f0ab0737789ae9524b989e9a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1779803786</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Intoxication">
  <data key="d0">Water Intoxication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Water intoxication is a medical condition resulting from the consumption of an excessive amount of water, typically over a short period. This over-hydration leads to a dangerous dilution of electrolytes in the body, disrupting homeostatic balance and impairing normal physiological functions. The condition is closely linked to electrolyte imbalance and is discussed in medical literature as a rare but serious disorder.

Symptoms of water intoxication include confusion, drowsiness, double vision, muscle cramps, and a pale or colorless appearance of the hands, feet, and lips. Affected individuals may also experience frequent urination and an altered mental state that can resemble alcohol intoxication. If left untreated, the condition can progress to severe outcomes such as coma and death. Due to its potentially fatal nature, water intoxication is a critical topic in health education and is frequently queried in medical and public health contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Water intoxication is a condition caused by excessive water intake, leading to dilution of body salts and electrolyte imbalance.&lt;SEP&gt;Water intoxication is a condition of excessive water intake, discussed as a topic in content creation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ead1494c17202662c334ce26d68202b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcaf9e38bb2a570a6edf70e6a9681dfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8122ad3e878784e98cdd0c33cb998553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c77ed812b87a04f08a3ce700769524d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46a5ce46cdcaba690c43278c43e6956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2002fbb248a146a783e2d25d0a26b5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22c59e2a7169d4f33e0aa485c94cdfc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b15cca57f0ab0737789ae9524b989e9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30f6de50b751c0769c7fedc8b9ca736c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c762de7be0b6a4d90e049c5181bbfa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d812dd7762edcda121f56954dea1223f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
