<node id="Boolean Question">
  <data key="d0">Boolean Question</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Boolean question is a type of query that expects a yes/no answer, used for precise anchor text.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of question that comes after a more unique question.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean question is a type of question used in the content structure, preceding other questions.&lt;SEP&gt;A boolean question is a yes/no interrogative used in the content, such as "Should you drink hot water daily?".&lt;SEP&gt;A Boolean question is a type of query that appears in the macro context of the article, used to directly address whether something is good or bad.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean Question is a type of question used in content briefs, requiring a yes/no or true/false answer.&lt;SEP&gt;A question that can be answered with yes/no, such as "is drinking cold water bad for you?".</data>
