<edge source="Macro Context" target="Micro Context">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Micro Context is written after the Macro Context as a supplementary section.&lt;SEP&gt;Micro context supplements the macro context with specific details.&lt;SEP&gt;The macro context and micro context are separated by a contextual border within the article.&lt;SEP&gt;The macro context and micro context must be connected via contextual vector to maintain semantic flow.&lt;SEP&gt;Macro context and micro context are used to organize content, with macro providing broad framework and micro providing details.</data>
